<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> A great story about my friend Dr. Sylvan Stool
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> (yes that was his real name)
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> When he was an intern, the child of the
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> chief of staff, a SOB neurosurgeon fell out
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> of the family car & was brought to the hospital.
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> Every staff physician was called in . Finally
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> Daddy got there. He asked, "Is the urine ok?"
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> Nobody had thought to order it.
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> Very important, as it is a test for internal bleeding.
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> Daddy turns to
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> Sylvan and says, "Stool, you are now in charge of this 
case"
<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> (There is a moral here that may relate to Hubble)
